#Aws
AWS stands for Amazon Web Services. It is a big cloud computing platform run by Amazon. It gives people and businesses online access to computer power, storage, and databases.

##Core AWS services-
-compute: **EC2**, Elasric, benstalk, lambda -Host apps and microservices
-storage: **S3**-file upload/download
-DB:**RDS**(mysql,postgres), DynanoDB-db storage
-Network-VPC, Route s3, ApiGateways- networking custom domain
-security- **IAM**, secret, managers, cognito- Auth and access controll
-mointoring- cloudwatch, X-ray- logs meterics and tracing
-CI/CD- codepipleline, codedeploy - deployment automation
-IAAS- AWS cloudformation/Terraform - infra as a code
-Containers- EC2,EKS,Fragate-dockerized apps
-Messaging- sqs, SNS, EventBridge - Async Processing
-serverless- **lambda**, springcloud foundation - lightweight serices

